<b><span style="font-size: 26px"><span style="color: #330066"><i>Biography</i></span></span><br>
<span style="color: #330066"><br>
<i><span style="font-size: 15px">Violent Vira (real name Vira) is an American singer and songwriter of Mexican descent. Born on August 27, 2000, in Boise, Idaho, she rose to fame in 2021 after the release of the viral single "I Don't Care," which garnered tens of millions of streams. In November 2025, she released her first full-length album, "Lover of a Ghost," under Mom+Pop Music. Initially a solo artist, she later formed a group in Dallas, consisting of members named Blank, Matt, and Anthony. She previously performed simply as Vira, but was forced to change her name to Violent Vira due to legal claims from a Spanish group of the same name.</span></i></span></b><br>
